<!--
  Thirteen URLs: every page that carries <meta name="robots" content="index,follow">.

  It used to carry two – the home page and bearings.html – so about.html and four
  of the five case studies were absent, and about.html is the single most
  name-relevant page on the site. A sitemap is a discovery hint, not a permission,
  so their absence did not block indexing; it just meant nothing here vouched for
  them.

  DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and they must stay absent: play.html and gradientlab.html
  are noindex. Listing a noindex URL here is a contradiction – the sitemap asks a
  crawler to index a page the page itself refuses – and Search Console reports it
  as an error against the whole file.

  The location values below are apex, no www, matching every canonical link on
  the site. NOTE that the live host currently 308-redirects apex -> www, which makes
  every URL in this file a redirect. See the audit at
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-seo-safari-audit.md: whichever way that is
  settled, this file, robots.txt and the ten canonicals have to agree with the
  server, and right now they do not.

  lastmod is each file's real last-commit date, not the day the sitemap was
  edited. A lastmod that moves when nothing changed is a signal crawlers learn to
  discount.
-->
